                  "obligationId": "scenario%3Aglobal-only-no-document-view::entry%3Ashare-create",
                  "decision": {
                    "kind": "observed",
                    "observed": "deny"
                  },
                  "branchResults": [],
                  "explanation": "At the declared ShareLinkViewSet.create boundary, the principal is the authenticated caller supplied to the serializer as request.user. The operation creates a ShareLink, while the protected target resource is the referenced document, not merely the new share-link object. The viewset exposes the create path through CreateModelMixin, uses ShareLinkSerializer, and applies IsAuthenticated plus PaperlessObjectPermissions. PassUserMixin supplies request.user to the serializer. During document validation, the serializer requires both the global documents.view_document permission and has_perms_owner_aware(..., \"view_document\", document). That owner-aware check permits the owner or an object permission, but not a caller who has only the global grant for another user's document. Under the stated premise that the caller lacks object view_document permission and does not own the document, validation raises PermissionDenied before the share link is created. Thus the source-visible behavior is deny and matches the accepted policy. No decisive runtime fact is missing within the declared-entry analysis because the question supplies the relevant identity, ownership, and object-permission premises; this result does not claim repository-wide or deployment completeness.",
                  "facts": [
